userStories.description:
**Goal** — Expose the authenticated user's or agent's effective global or project keys for fail-closed web gating.

**Motivation** — The API decides every request on permission keys since enforce-core, and roles are data: a Triager, an Approver or any custom role is a first-class binding.

**Approach** — New controller `MePermissionsController` in `apps/api/src/projects/me-permissions.controller.ts`, registered in `ProjectsModule` (it needs `ProjectAccessService`; `PermissionsModule` is global, so the controller cannot live there without importing `ProjectsModule`).

```ts
@ApiTags('permissions')
@ApiBearerAuth()
@Controller('me/permissions')
export class MePermissionsController {
  constructor(private readonly access: ProjectAccessService, private readonly permissions: PermissionService) {}

  @Get()
  @UseGuards(RequiresGuard)
  @Requires('auth.me.read')            // implicit: every authenticated principal holds it
  async read(@Query() query: MePermissionsQuery, @Principal() principal: KodaPrincipal) { ... }
}
```

- `MePermissionsQuery { project?: string }` (a project slug, `IsString` and `IsNotEmpty` when present: `?project=` with an empty value is a 400 validation error). A runner never reaches this route: `CombinedAuthGuard` keeps runner keys on `@RunnerRoute()` routes.
- Without `project`: `PermissionService.effectiveKeys(ref, 'global')`.
- With `project`: `ProjectAccessService.findProjectIdBySlug(slug)` (404 `projects`), then `ProjectAccessService.resolveMembership(projectId, principal)` (403 `projects` when the caller lacks `project.read` there), then `PermissionService.effectiveKeys(ref, { projectId })`.
- Response `MePermissionsDto { scope: 'global' | 'project'; projectSlug: string | null; keys: string[] }`, `keys` sorted ascending. The set is exactly what `effectiveKeys` returns: role-derived keys and `X.own` entries, never implicit or public keys.
- `ref` is `{ type: 'USER' | 'AGENT', id }` from the principal, as `PermissionService.can` builds it.

**Scope** — In: controller, DTOs, ProjectsModule registration, integration behavior and endpoint e2e inventory case, preserving existing controllers and cases. Out: catalog/filter changes (US-002), browser composables (US-006), spec export (US-005). `/me/permissions` lists role-derived keys only; implicit and public keys are always allowed by the API and are not listed.

**Interface** — `PermissionService.effectiveKeys(principal: PrincipalRef, scope: PermissionScope): Promise<ReadonlySet<string>>`; `MePermissionsQuery { project?: string }`; `MePermissionsDto { scope: 'global' | 'project'; projectSlug: string | null; keys: string[] }`.
